Third-party crates
------------------
A shipped binary carries third-party crates, and ATTRIBUTION.md names every one this workspace
resolves together with the licence it declares. That file is GENERATED - `just attribution` writes
it and `cargo xtask check-attribution` fails when it falls behind Cargo.lock - so it cannot quietly
fall out of step with what is built.

What it does not carry is the notice text of each dependency: an Apache-2.0 crate's own NOTICE file
lives in its source tree rather than in its metadata. The per-release licence review, produced by
the release workflow and signed like every other asset, is the curated second opinion; see
docs/verifying-a-release.md.

Vendored code
-------------
Code derived from an upstream project retains its original licence header and is recorded
in VENDOR.md with the upstream repository, commit, date and the local modifications made.
REUSE.toml records its licence per file. The two crates under vendor/mimalloc_rust are path
dependencies rather than registry ones, so they are attributed there and not in ATTRIBUTION.md.
